-# One job: checkout (shallow), build, gate, deploy, tag, measure. Target: push to served in about 40 s (PIPELINE.md section 3).
+# Three jobs, each at its own altitude (library/altitudes.md, "Grants and crossings"; incident.ci@'s patch, 11 November):
+#   build  (contents: read; checkout keeps no credential): checkout (shallow), gate, generators, the brief's PDFs, the site as an artifact;
+#   deploy (pages: write, id-token: write; no checkout, no repository code): deploys that artifact, measures push to served;
+#   tag    (contents: write; no checkout, no repository code): the version tag, through the API.
+# Target: push to served in about 40 s (PIPELINE.md section 3).
 #   - fetch-depth 1 and nothing reads git history (a blobless full clone made the team site's gate 40x slower);
 #   - the newest push wins among the waiting runs; a running deploy is never cancelled (with agents pushing every few
 #     seconds, cancelling starved the site: nothing was served until pushes paused);
@@ -16,20 +20,19 @@
